        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "A length of steel bar stock of suitable diameter is mounted in the chuck. Two collars are machined on the work piece; one collar near the chuck jaws, the other collar at the free end of the bar.",
            "block_bbox": [
                504,
                668,
                894,
                780
            ],
            "block_id": 17,
            "block_order": 10,
            "group_id": 17
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The next step is to take a very light finishing cut across one collar, and without changing the adjustment of the tool, the cut is continued across the other collar. The diameter of each collar should be the same, otherwise a taper is indicated. The tolerance allowed is shown in Fig. 26.72.",
